Volvo Reman remanufactures components to original OEM specifications by factory-trained technicians, reusing 85% of original material while consuming 80% less energy than new manufacture. Remanufactured parts deliver identical performance to new while supporting Volvo's lifecycle cost positioning. This strategy extends heavy equipment economic lifespan, addresses cost sensitivity in markets with lower income, and positions remanufactured components as premium quality choice through OEM brand association rather than value positioning.